# Purchased LimeZu art. The licence permits use but not redistribution.
# See docs/04-ART-DIRECTION.md.
#
# Note this ignores the *contents*, not the directory. `assets/` on its own
# excludes the directory wholesale, and git cannot re-include a file inside an
# excluded directory — the negation below would silently do nothing.
assets/*

# ...except the manifest, which is the contract the scene builds against. It
# holds filenames and numbers, no artwork, so tracking it redistributes nothing.
# Without it a fresh clone cannot build the scene at all, and M5's "final art
# drops in as a manifest swap with zero code change" is only reviewable if the
# manifest is in the history. Regenerate with scripts/build-manifest.py.
!assets/manifest.json

.build/
.swiftpm/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
.DS_Store

__pycache__/
*.pyc
